{% comment %}
  Free-shipping message that is market-aware (audit issue #16).

  - Only renders for Ireland (IE) and the United Kingdom (GB).
  - Hidden for every other country/market, so the hardcoded euro figure
    never shows to shoppers browsing in another currency (e.g. PHP).
  - Ireland and the UK each show their own threshold/text.

  Detection uses the shopper's active country (localization.country.iso_code),
  which follows the Shopify Market they are browsing in.

  EDIT THE TWO MESSAGES BELOW to match your live shipping policy.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign country = localization.country.iso_code

  assign ie_message = 'Free Shipping Over €150'
  assign uk_message = 'Free Shipping Over £130'

  assign message = ''
  if country == 'IE'
    assign message = ie_message
  elsif country == 'GB'
    assign message = uk_message
  endif
-%}

{%- if message != blank -%}
  <h3 class="rich-text__heading heading h6 free-shipping-message">{{ message }}</h3>
{%- endif -%}
